      "role": "hook",
      "headline": "More than 20 emperors in about 50 years. Most of them were murdered."
    },
    {
      "id": "card.ancient_rome.081.c2",
      "type": "text",
      "role": "explain",
      "headline": "Everything at once",
      "body": "From 235 to 284 CE, the Crisis of the Third Century, the empire suffered civil wars, invasions, plague and economic trouble. Emperors had reduced the silver in the denarius until it held very little, and prices soared."
    },
    {
      "id": "card.ancient_rome.081.c3",
      "type": "text",
      "role": "explain",
      "headline": "An emperor in chains",
      "body": "In 260 CE the emperor Valerian was captured by the Persian king Shapur I, the first Roman emperor taken prisoner by a foreign enemy. For a time the empire split into three, with a Gallic Empire in the west and Palmyra under Queen Zenobia in the east."
    },
    {
      "id": "card.ancient_rome.081.c4",
      "type": "fact",
      "fact": "Aurelian put the pieces back together.",
      "context": "In the 270s he reunited the empire and built new walls around Rome itself."
    },
